   160	
   161	No revision is enacted here. Each question in section 5 has its own answer; an umbrella approval cannot choose these independently.
   162	
   163	| Rows | Scope and status | Question |
   164	|---|---|---|
   165	| OD126; Q3.7/Q3.9/Q3.10 | Generalize address/profile interface, preserving provenance rules and zero-byte exception; existing 64-bit little-endian profile unchanged, including Q3.10’s `base + size ≤ 2^64−1` one-past bound. Any generalized profile needs an analogous checked bound. | 3 |
   166	| Q3.5; Q1.11/Q2.4/Q4.6; TYPE-19; FFI-7 | Q3.5 fixes u64 lengths/indices across profiles. Q1.11 rejects counts above u64 as TooLarge; Q2.4 fixes Drained.at: u64; Q4.6 byte offsets/lengths use that index contract. Target-sized usize would revise these and layout-query results. Recommendation retains these semantics and permits only proved narrower representations. | 7 |
   167	| OD126; FFI-7 | Native enum tag/payload layout changes existing i32-tag profile separately from target abstraction. | 4 |
   168	| Q1.7 | Proved release-context erasure, including owning Text where applicable; no unconditional one-pointer claim. | 6 |
   169	| Q7.1/Q7.10; Q9.7 | Lawful registry instances rather than a permanently closed inventory; preserve existing grant contracts. Entropy details deferred. | 16, 14 |
   170	| FFI-7/10 | Natural native struct layout already supersedes unspecified-layout prose under runtime decision; retain repr restrictions. | Retained clarification |
   171	| Q8.1; early-evidence decision; R-0505 | Keep current conditional endpoint and later closure; advancing it requires separate approval. | 8 |
   172	
   173	Q9.11/OD144 already decide post-cleanup ensures timing. The SPARK decision already decides source struct invariants. Neither is a new rule. C4’s hybrid/representation completion is a proposed formalization choice, not authority to revise raw access. Exact trap constructors and byte columns are not inferred from Q6.7 or ArithmeticError. OD106/ARITH-10 already fix conversion errors; Q2.3 and Q3.8 already fix destruction orders. Questions 12 and 13 are removed as fully decided; later question numbers are retained for review tracking.
