   686	## 3. Proofs
   687	
   688	### 3.1 Interaction and integration proofs for A2i
   689	
   690	1. **Borrow across deferred cleanup** (`defer_holds_loan`). Covered cases:
   691	   - A deferred call's borrowed arguments keep their root locked from registration until the call
   692	     runs. Its by-value arguments are read when it runs.
   693	   - On a **successful** unwind (fall-through, `break L`, `continue L` or `return`): the exit value
   694	     is evaluated first; each call comes before its own loan ends; the scope's loans end after its
   695	     deferred calls; locals are destroyed last.
