   141	    foreign calls stay visible, so a bounded, analyzable core can be told apart from an effectful
   142	    shell, and writing code that way is natural. Before a program runs, every function has
   143	    termination evidence with its premises, or a report naming the explicitly permitted unresolved
   144	    obligations: every loop, recursive cycle, indirect call and blocking or foreign boundary either has termination
   145	    evidence or carries a written permission at that source, which every report traces to its
   146	    callers. Recursion depth, stack use, allocation, blocking, foreign calls and possible aborts are
   147	    reported per function with their evidence, and a module or project policy may require them;
   148	    these are reported facts, not function categories
   149	    ([decision](decisions.md#decided-project-no-hidden-traps), 2026-11-06). *Why:* resource bounds
   150	    and proofs need a core they can reach, and an unexplained infinite loop is a hidden behaviour.
     1	# Concrete Lean foundation
     2	
     3	Status: approved by the owner 2026-11-08; the plan for PLAN steps 3+; the Lean spec stays the only home of rules.
     4	
     5	The owner approved writing the shared foundation before the freeze on 2026-11-07, **"ok to option b then for freeze the foundation>?"**, and answered every question of section 5 with its recommendation on 2026-11-08, **"ok all recommended"**. Both answers are recorded in [decisions.md](../decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-foundation), which is the home of the decisions; ROADMAP R-0607 to R-0616 hold the work. The text below is the approved draft 3: where it says a recommendation, proposal or question, the recommendation is what the owner approved, and the revisions of section 4 are enacted as decisions.md records them. Questions 12 and 13 were removed as already decided. This document states no rule of its own: each contract becomes Lean definitions and theorems in [ConcreteSpec](../../ConcreteSpec/README.md).
     6	
     7	The [A2i decision](../decisions.md#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06) freezes integrated scopes, "not an untested whole-language architecture". Here the frozen foundation means interfaces and laws implemented, proved and tested together, with representative interactions. It does not mean designing every future slice before slice 1. Later slices supply lawful instances; changes to decided rules return to the owner.
     8	
     9	References below use the actual anchors in this checkout. **Core rows** means [Q1–Q9](../decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core). The pipeline referred to in the brief as the 2026-11-07 decision is recorded here under [the 2026-11-06 pipeline anchor](../decisions.md#decided-project-pipeline-2026-11-06); there is no `decided-2026-11-07-pipeline` anchor. The [authoritative core-row notes](../archive/decisions-2026-11-05/core_rows.json) supplement these rows. Proposed additions without a decided row are identified as such.
    10	
    11	## 1. The freeze boundary
